    "failure_scenario": "In a long session where the user selects a file then navigates back/forward without submitting or cancelling, the blob URL remains allocated in browser memory. While a single 2MB blob is not catastrophic, this is a classic React memory leak pattern. Adding a useEffect(() => () => { if (previewUrl) URL.revokeObjectURL(previewUrl); }, [previewUrl]) would guarantee cleanup. The handleCancel and handleFileSelect paths handle explicit user actions but miss the unmount path entirely."
  },
