    "file": "frontend/src/api/client.ts",
    "line": 26,
    "summary": "The request interceptor unconditionally sets Content-Type to application/json for all non-FormData requests, overwriting any Content-Type the caller may have explicitly set (e.g., text/plain for a text body, or multipart/related). This happens on every request, not just ones without a Content-Type.",
    "failure_scenario": "If a future API call needs to send text/plain or application/xml (e.g., a markdown editor save endpoint), the interceptor will silently overwrite the caller's Content-Type with application/json. The backend would receive a mismatched header and potentially fail to parse the body. The fix is to only set Content-Type when it is not already present: if (!config.headers.getContentType?.()) { config.headers['Content-Type'] = 'application/json'; }."
